{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtVn4qVYPb5SkmeRH37F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added the `codex-sandboxed` lane to `run.sh`. It runs the same `codex exec` as the `codex` lane, with the Codex process under `sandbox/agent.sb`, and I wrote up the details in `ANSWER.md`. I have not run it against a live model, so the first real run is still to do.\n\n**What the lane does**\n- It copies `auth.json` and `config.toml` from the real `~/.codex` into a scratch `CODEX_HOME` in `/tmp`, before the sandbox starts. Then it runs codex with that scratch home.\n- It passes `-o` a file in a scratch folder in `/tmp`. After the run, it copies that file to `final.txt` in the run folder. If codex exits 0 but writes no file, the lane logs an error and exits 1.\n\n**Why the scratch home needs the login**\nCodex does not authenticate from an environment variable on this machine. `CODEX_API_KEY` is not set, and the `codex` lane logs in from `~/.codex/auth.json`. A scratch home with nothing in it would break auth, so the lane seeds it with the login and config. I also corrected a README paragraph that said Codex needs nothing from the home folder, which was wrong here.\n\n**Trade-offs**\n- The agent's shell can read the copied `auth.json` in `/tmp`. The kimi lane has the same exposure for `~/.kimi-code`.\n- The MCP server in `config.toml` that lives under the real home will not start inside this lane. The `codex` lane does not have that problem, so the two lanes do not expose identical tools.\n\n**Verification**\n- `bash -n` passes.\n- Under the profile, reads and writes to the real `~/.codex` are denied, scratch writes work, and `codex login status` reports a ChatGPT login.\n- With a fake `codex` on `PATH`, the lane produced the expected files in both the success case and the missing-output case. I removed the test artifacts afterwards.\n\nI did not run a live Codex job, because it would send the fizz task to the model provider and you did not ask for that. The `-o` failure from your colleague's note did not reproduce here, because this checkout is outside the home folder. The README says the harness normally lives under the home folder, so I kept the scratch-folder design.\n\nNothing is committed. Changes are in `run.sh`, `README.md`, and the new `ANSWER.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3785,"cache_read_input_tokens":45483,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3785},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"85f5ac4d-14b2-446b-820a-cb8a79ccb8f7","uuid":"8a545e03-3582-4616-8f4c-8354017ad472","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:57:38.025Z","request_id":"req_011CgtVn4gKFkKYHZgVZnuWk"}
